<title>POLAND: Kredyt Bank delays new share issue.</title>
<headline>Kredyt Bank delays new share issue.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's Kredyt Bank SA has delayed by two weeks the subscription period for its 10 million new shares to 21-25 April, the bank said in a statement on Friday.</p>
<p>Kredyt Bank has also put off by one week until May 5-6 the subscription for shares earmarked for the European Bank for Reconstruction and Development (EBRD).</p>
<p>The bank said it was moving the subscriptions until after the release of audited 1996 results.</p>
<p> Tranches		  No Of Shares	   Subscription</p>
<p>			     Offered		  Period</p>
<p> Large-investor	  10,000,000	     April 21-25</p>
<p> Small-investor	   2,000,000	     April 21-25</p>
<p> EBRD tranche		 847,000	     May 5-6</p>
<p> Price(PLN):		    8</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
